#!/bin/bash
#
# Refuses a commit that adds an asset without its .meta file, or a .meta without its asset (a missing .meta
# makes Unity mint a new GUID on the next machine and breaks every reference to the asset).
# new-game.ps1 enables it with: git config core.hooksPath .githooks
#
# From https://github.com/doitian/unity-git-hooks (scripts/pre-commit). One local change below this header: the
# index is read once into an associative array (in_index) instead of one `git ls-files` per path and directory
# level, so committing a vendored pack (Assets/Feel, thousands of files) takes seconds, not thousands of process
# spawns. Unlike a git pathspec, in_index matches names literally ([ and * are not globs). Ceiling: macOS's
# /bin/bash 3.2 has no associative arrays, so there it falls back to the upstream per-path git call.
#
